# Bug Report: Anonymizer Script Crashes and Inconsistent Behavior

## Description
The anonymizer script can crash or behave unexpectedly in several cases:

- Throws an error for JSXNamespacedName instead of handling it gracefully:

JSXNamespacedName(path) {
  throw error('TODO: handle JSXNamespacedName');
}

- Duplicate logic in identifier/literal anonymization increases risk of bugs:

Identifier(path) {
  const name = path.node.name;
  if (BUILTIN_HOOKS.has(name) || GLOBALS.has(name)) return;
  // repeated logic for generating new names
}

- Random string generation for literals is inconsistent:

StringLiteral(path) {
  let string = '';
  while (string.length < value.length) {
    string += String.fromCharCode(Math.round(Math.random() * 58) + 65);
  }
  path.node.value = string;
}

- File reading or parsing errors are uncaught:

text = fs.readFileSync(file, 'utf8');

## Expected Behavior
Script should handle all JSX nodes safely, generate consistent anonymized identifiers/literals, and provide clear error messages.

## Actual Behavior
Crashes on certain JSX nodes, inconsistent anonymized output, and uncaught errors when reading files or stdin.

## Environment
- Node.js version: [v20.19.2]
- OS: [debian 13]

When using following code:
```
