### Any additional comments?

When the following CSS is written:

```html
<style scoped>
	.class {
		> * {
			background-color: blue;
		}
  }
</style>
```

It used to be compiled to the following, in Vue 3.5.14:

```css
.class {
> *[data-v-7ba5bd90] {
			background-color: blue;
}
}
```

In Vue 3.5.15, it is compiled to this instead:

```css
.class {
[data-v-7ba5bd90]> [data-v-7ba5bd90] {
			background-color: blue;
}
}
```

In practice, this results in two problems:
- It means this generated CSS expects one or more elements between the `.class` and `div` (`.class
[data-v-7ba5bd90] > [data-v-7ba5bd90]` instead of `.class > [data-v-7ba5bd90]`).
- It causes a regression in specificity. Before, it had a specificity of `0-... [TRUNCATED]

