### Description


Angular supports class inheritance for components and directives, but the derived component still has to provide its own template. In practice, this makes extension of third-party or open-source components much harder than it could be.

A child component can inherit inputs, outputs, host bindings, and class logic, but it cannot reuse the already defined template of the base/existing component in a compiler-supported way.

This becomes especially painful when I want to slightly customize behavior of an existing component from a library, while still keeping its original HTML template and future template updates.


