### Description

When a custom Signal Forms control defines a `focus()` method, calling `field().focusBoundControl()` invokes that method with a lost `this` context.

If `focus()` reads instance members (for example a `viewChild` signal), it throws at runtime.

```ts
@Component({
  selector: 'custom-control',
  host: {'tabindex': '-1'},
  template: '<input #input />',
})
class CustomControl {
  readonly value = model<string>();
  readonly input = viewChild.required<ElementRef<HTMLInputElement>>('input');

  focus() {
    // Fails when called
    this.input().nativeElement.focus();
  }
}

@Component({
  imports: [FormField, CustomControl],
  template: `<custom-control [formField]="f" />`,
})
class TestCmp {
  readonly f = form(signal(''));
}

it('repro', async () => {
  const fixture = TestBed.createComponent(TestCmp);
  await fixture.whenStable();
  // Throws: TypeError: this.input is not a function
  fixture.componentInstance.f().focusBoundControl();
});
```


