### Describe the bug

Since svelte version [`5.53.7`](https://github.com/sveltejs/svelte/releases/tag/svelte%405.53.7), the content of the `#if` block is evaluated before the condition of the `#if` block, so you can't rely on it to catch undefined values for example.

In previous versions (`5.53.6` and lower), i could rely on the fact that inside of the outer `#if` block, `value` is always an array.

```svelte
<script lang="ts">
	import {slide} from 'svelte/transition';

	let value: {current: number}[] | undefined = $state([{current: 1}]);
</script>

<button
	onclick={() => {
		if (value) {
			value = undefined;
		} else {
			value = [{current: 1}];
		}
	}}
>
	toggle
</button>

{#if value?.length}
	<div transition:slide>
		{#if value[0]?.current}
			x
		{/if}
	</div>
{/if}
```

### Reproduction

https://svelte.dev/playground/042eda8e56f2493faa3cc5ffc78dac85?version=5.53.7

1. Turn off async mode
2. Click on toggle
3. Error is produced in console and everything breaks

When you remove the transition, it works fine.
In versions `5.53.6` and lower, it works even with the transition.


