### Describe the problem

I find myself more often in the position of writing `OPTIONS` endpoints. To make that easier, I wrote a small helper function — similar to `json()` and `text()` — to return a `204 No Content` response more quickly and cleanly.

Maybe this could just be added to the SvelteKit core too?

It just feels so much nicer for my eyes to **always return a function**, instead of sometimes calling a function (`json()`, `text()`) and other times manually instantiating a `Response` object. It makes the code feel more consistent and ergonomic overall. Maybe some of you feel the same way.

### Describe the proposed solution

Right now i use:

```js
/**
 * Create a `Response` object `No Content`. 
 * @param {ResponseInit} [init]  Options such as `status` and `headers` that will be added to the response.
 */
export function empty(init?: ResponseInit) {
  const headers = new Headers(init?.headers);
  return new Response(null, {
    ...init,
    headers,
    status: 204
  });
}
```
or general-purpose
```js
/**
 * Creates a `Response` object with the given body and initialization options.
 * @param {BodyInit | null} body - The body of the response. Can be a string, Blob, ArrayBuffer, FormData, etc., or `null` for no body.
 * @param {ResponseInit} [init] - Optional response options such as status, headers, and statusText.
 */
export function empty(body, init) {
  const headers = new Headers(init?.headers);
  return new Response(body, {
      ...init,
      headers
  });
}... [TRUNCATED]

### Describe the bug

When I have following code:

```js
let map = new SvelteMap()
map.set("svelte", { counter: 0})

const obj = map.get("svelte")

obj.counter += 1

map.set(name, obj)
```

`map.set("svelte", { counter: 0})` triggers a reactive change, while `map.set(name, obj)` does not.

