Setting `server.servlet.session.cookie.partitioned=false` still produces `; Partitioned` on the session cookie. This is a regression from the fix for #50201 (commit b02f7dd, first released in 4.0.7).

In `ServletContextInitializers.SessionConfiguringInitializer.configureSessionCookie`:

```java
map.from(cookie::getPartitioned).to((partitioned) -> config.setAttribute("Partitioned", ""));
```

`PropertyMapper.to(...)` only filters `null`, so `Boolean.FALSE` reaches the consumer. The lambda then ignores the actual Boolean value and always sets the `Partitioned` attribute to `""`. Tomcat's `Rfc6265CookieProcessor` emits `; Partitioned` when the attribute is `""`, so an explicit `false` is rendered the same as `true`. The attribute is set by the container-agnostic `ServletContextInitializers`, so the same mapping applies to Jetty.

The #50201 fix also changed `AbstractServletWebServerFactoryTests.sessionConfiguration`, which sets `partitioned=false`, to assert `getAttribute("Partitioned")).isEqualTo("")`. That checks the internal attribute value, not the resulting `Set-Cookie` header.

