**Spring Boot version:** main

When a Cloud Foundry security check fails (expired token, access denied, etc.), the reactive `SecureReactiveWebOperation` returns only the HTTP status code with no response body:

```java
// CloudFoundryWebFluxEndpointHandlerMapping.SecureReactiveWebOperation
if (!securityResponse.getStatus().equals(HttpStatus.OK)) {
    return Mono.just(new ResponseEntity<>(securityResponse.getStatus()));
}
```

The servlet counterpart includes a `{"security_error":"..."}` body:

```java
// CloudFoundryWebEndpointServletHandlerMapping.SecureServletWebOperation
if (!securityResponse.getStatus().equals(HttpStatus.OK)) {
    return new ResponseEntity<Object>(securityResponse.getMessage(), securityResponse.getStatus());
}
```

The message takes the form `{"security_error":"Access denied"}` or `{"security_error":"Token expired"}` — information that `SecurityInterceptor` already computes but the reactive path silently discards.

**Expected behavior:** A failed Cloud Foundry security check in a WebFlux application returns the same `{"security_error":"<reason>"}` body as the servlet counterpart.

**Actual behavior:** Only the status code (401, 403, 503) is returned with an empty body.

I'd be happy to contribute a fix for this.

